  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.5.0 — New: gradual intra refresh. Set IntraRefreshPeriodFrames and a recovery request during IDR cooldown starts a wave of intra macroblock columns sweeping the picture, with constrained_intra_pred_flag and motion vectors restricted to the refreshed region, so a decoder joining at the wave start reconstructs byte-exactly once the wave completes — bounded per-frame cost instead of an IDR-sized spike (worst frame ~3x a typical P, versus ~14x for an IDR). Off by default and byte-identical when off. BREAKING: IIntraRefreshPolicy and IntraRefreshPolicyStub are removed; the feature lives on the encoder, and EncoderAdaptationDecision.EnableIntraRefresh now has an effect. Fixed: RTT congestion detection used an absolute 50 ms threshold, so any link with a baseline RTT above that was permanently treated as congested and pinned to the bitrate floor; it now tracks a baseline and CongestionRttMultiplier is finally wired. EncoderPipelineStats motion/texture/scene-change signals are measured rather than hardcoded zeros, and drive a scene-change IDR. Removed the Queue namespace, whose drop policy could never fire as composed. Variance kernels are SIMD (~6x on the adaptive-quant path). Single-frame encoding is byte-identical to 0.4.0.",
